---
import ComparisonPageLayout from '../../layouts/ComparisonPageLayout.astro';

// Competitor facts checked against GitHub's docs, changelog and the
// github/copilot-cli repo on 2026-10-11. Research notes:
// docs/research/2026-10-11-competitive-landscape-refresh.md
const comparison = {
  competitor: {
    name: 'GitHub Copilot CLI',
    icon: '🐙',
    tagline: 'GitHub\'s agentic coding CLI',
    description: 'GitHub Copilot CLI is a terminal coding agent. It went GA in February 2026 and replaced the retired gh copilot extension.'
  },
  tldr: {
    title: 'TL;DR',
    points: [
      'Copilot CLI uses GitHub-hosted models by default. Since April 2026 it can also run offline with your own or local models, if you configure it.',
      'Caro fetches its local model once, automatically, and then runs offline by default. No account, no API key, no provider setup.',
      'Caro checks every command against 52+ built-in dangerous-command patterns with risk levels. Copilot CLI asks before risky commands and lets you write allow/deny rules, but ships no built-in pattern library.',
      'Copilot CLI has an OS-level sandbox (GA in October 2026, off until you turn it on). Caro checks commands before they run and does not sandbox them.',
      'Copilot CLI is proprietary. Caro is open source (AGPL-3.0).'
    ]
  },
  headToHead: [
    { feature: 'Open source', caro: true, competitor: false, winner: 'caro' },
    { feature: 'Works offline', caro: true, competitor: 'partial', winner: 'caro' },
    { feature: 'Local model set up for you', caro: true, competitor: false, winner: 'caro' },
    { feature: 'No account needed', caro: true, competitor: 'partial', winner: 'caro' },
    { feature: 'Built-in dangerous-command patterns', caro: true, competitor: false, winner: 'caro' },
    { feature: 'Risk level for each command', caro: true, competitor: false, winner: 'caro' },
    { feature: 'Your own allow/deny rules', caro: true, competitor: true, winner: 'tie' },
    { feature: 'Uses your existing terminal', caro: true, competitor: true, winner: 'tie' },
    { feature: 'OS-level sandbox', caro: false, competitor: true, winner: 'competitor' },
    { feature: 'Full coding agent (edits files, runs tasks)', caro: false, competitor: true, winner: 'competitor' },
    { feature: 'Hosted frontier models', caro: false, competitor: true, winner: 'competitor' },
  ],
  sections: [
    {
      title: 'Privacy and Offline Use',
      icon: '🔒',
      content: `
        <p><strong>GitHub Copilot CLI</strong> sends prompts to GitHub-hosted models by default, and usage telemetry is on by default. Since April 2026 you can bring your own key or point it at a local model (Ollama, vLLM, Foundry Local). With <code>COPILOT_OFFLINE=true</code> and a local model, it makes no calls to GitHub and needs no GitHub login.</p>
        <p><strong>Caro</strong> is offline by default. It downloads its local model once, on first use, and needs no network after that. Prompts and commands stay on your machine.</p>
      `
    },
    {
      title: 'Safety Approach',
      icon: '🛡️',
      content: `
        <p><strong>GitHub Copilot CLI</strong> runs read-only shell commands on its own and asks before others. You can write deterministic rules such as <code>--deny-tool 'shell(rm)'</code>, and deny rules win even under <code>--allow-all</code>. Hooks can call an external validator, and an OS sandbox can limit files, network and credentials. It does not ship a curated list of dangerous commands.</p>
        <p><strong>Caro</strong> checks every command against 52+ curated patterns, rates it CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM or LOW, and blocks critical commands such as <code>rm -rf /</code>, with no configuration. A sandbox and a pattern check stop different things, so they work well together.</p>
      `
    },
    {
      title: 'Cost and Access',
      icon: '💰',
      content: `
        <p><strong>GitHub Copilot CLI</strong> is included in every Copilot plan, Copilot Free included. Paid plans run from $10 to $100 per month for individuals and $19 to $39 per seat for organizations. Since June 2026, usage is billed in AI Credits. In bring-your-own-key mode you pay your model provider.</p>
        <p><strong>Caro</strong> is free and open source. You run it on your own hardware. No account, no subscription, no usage limit.</p>
      `
    },
    {
      title: 'Scope and Model Quality',
      icon: '🧠',
      content: `
        <p><strong>GitHub Copilot CLI</strong> is a full coding agent. It edits files, runs multi-step tasks, uses MCP servers and custom agents, and can switch between Anthropic, OpenAI and Google models. For complex or novel work, hosted frontier models are stronger than small local ones.</p>
        <p><strong>Caro</strong> does one job: turn a request into one safe shell command. Small local models handle common shell work well, and Caro adds platform detection and GNU/BSD awareness on top.</p>
      `
    },
  ],
  verdict: {
    chooseCaro: [
      'You want offline AI without configuring a model provider',
      'You work in air-gapped or compliance-restricted environments',
      'You want a built-in safety library with risk levels, not only rules you write',
      'You want open source with no account or subscription',
      'You want a quick command, not an agent session',
    ],
    chooseCompetitor: [
      'You want a full coding agent in the terminal',
      'You already pay for GitHub Copilot',
      'You want hosted frontier models from several vendors',
      'You want an OS-level sandbox around the agent',
    ]
  },
  verification: {
    date: '2026-10-11',
    sources: [
      { label: 'GitHub changelog: Copilot CLI is generally available (Feb 25, 2026)', url: 'https://github.blog/changelog/2026-02-25-github-copilot-cli-is-now-generally-available/' },
      { label: 'GitHub changelog: Copilot CLI supports BYOK and local models (Apr 7, 2026)', url: 'https://github.blog/changelog/2026-04-07-copilot-cli-now-supports-byok-and-local-models/' },
      { label: 'GitHub docs: allowing and denying tools', url: 'https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/copilot-cli/use-copilot-cli/allowing-tools' },
      { label: 'GitHub docs: responsible use of Copilot CLI', url: 'https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/responsible-use/copilot-cli' },
      { label: 'github/copilot-cli license', url: 'https://github.com/github/copilot-cli/blob/main/LICENSE.md' },
      { label: 'GitHub docs: Copilot plans', url: 'https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/get-started/plans' },
      { label: 'GitHub changelog: local sandboxing generally available (Oct 7, 2026)', url: 'https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-07-local-sandboxing-for-gitHub-copilot-now-generally-available' },
    ]
  }
};
---

<ComparisonPageLayout
  title="Caro vs GitHub Copilot CLI - Feature Comparison | Shell AI Tools"
  description="Compare Caro and GitHub Copilot CLI. An open-source, offline-by-default shell CLI with built-in safety patterns vs GitHub's agentic coding CLI."
  comparison={comparison}
  heroSubtitle="Offline-by-default shell companion vs GitHub's coding agent"
  finalCtaHeading="Ready for a Privacy-First Shell Companion?"
  finalCtaSubtext="Try Caro today. No account required. Privacy-first."
>
  <p slot="competitor-note" class="competitor-note">Already using Copilot CLI? Caro runs next to it for quick, offline commands.</p>
</ComparisonPageLayout>

<style>
  .competitor-note {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
